  "term": "logistic regression",
  "definition": "Logistic regression is a statistical method for finding the mathematical relationship between a qualitative dependent variable and one or more independent variables. It estimates the best-fitting relationship by using likelihood functions rather than the straight-line, least-squares approach used in linear regression.",
